From: Nitin Punn <ntipun@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12/wgl: fall back to an HWND swapchain when DirectComposition is unavailable

d3d12_wgl_framebuffer_resize() presents alpha pixel formats through a
DirectComposition visual. On platforms where dcomp.dll is a stub (Wine
on macOS with D3DMetal, for instance) dcomp_get_device() fails and the
function returns early, so the window never gets a swapchain and nothing
is ever presented, while the application sees no GL error at all.

Fall back to DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE and a regular CreateSwapChainForHwnd
in that case. Alpha compositing against the desktop is lost, which no GL
application relies on, but rendering becomes visible.

Seen with Foundation (Steam 690830) requesting a cAlphaBits=8 format.

--- a/src/gallium/winsys/d3d12/wgl/d3d12_wgl_framebuffer.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/d3d12/wgl/d3d12_wgl_framebuffer.cpp
@@ -165,6 +165,17 @@
    desc.SampleDesc.Count = 1;
    desc.AlphaMode = util_format_has_alpha(templ->format) ?
       DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_PREMULTIPLIED : DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE;
+
+   /* Presenting a format with alpha goes through DirectComposition. When
+    * DComp is unavailable (e.g. Wine only stubs it) fall back to a plain
+    * HWND swapchain instead of leaving the window without a swapchain. */
+   if (desc.AlphaMode != DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE && !framebuffer->dcomp) {
+      IDCompositionDevice *dev = dcomp_get_device();
+      if (dev)
+         framebuffer->dcomp.Attach(dev);
+      else
+         desc.AlphaMode = DXGI_ALPHA_MODE_IGNORE;
+   }
    desc.SwapEffect = DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_FLIP_SEQUENTIAL;
    desc.Scaling = DXGI_SCALING_STRETCH;
 
